// A model council with role-bound members and typed disagreement (roadmap item
// 516, `docs/design/543-model-council.md`).
//
// A council is several models answering the same question, each PLACED
// separately. That is the whole point of the construct: a local adversary may
// read an origin the cloud proposer may not, and item 514's ceiling decides
// that per member rather than per council. So a member is a pair — what it is
// FOR (`proposer`, `adversary`, `verifier`) and WHERE it runs (an item-512
// `model role`).
//
// The aggregation is WRITTEN DOWN, because the rule that turns three answers
// into one outcome is the council. `unanimous` names one value or names none,
// and naming none is `split`, which carries the members' differing answers as
// evidence. Nothing here resolves a disagreement toward an answer: a council
// that degrades to "whichever member answered" is strictly worse than one
// model, because the caller believes several agreed.
//
// The floor is counted over the DECLARED members and never over the ones that
// answered. A member that fails or times out abstains, and an abstention counts
// against the floor rather than toward agreement, so a council cannot shrink
// itself into a quorum.
//
// The declaration is checked at admission and contributes NOTHING to the IR:
// this file emits byte for byte what it would emit with the council deleted.
//
// This file is also the self-host's ADMITTING reproducer. The gate built from
// `selfhost/lower.rvl` answered every council program `BAD|unexpected token at
// top level` until the declaration was ported; it now admits this one and
// refuses `examples/rejections/gcouncilsplit_on_tie_allow.rvl` beside it
// with the reference's own message.

model role edge on_device
model role local2 on_device
model role vast off_device

service Answer {
  fn classify(text: Str) -> Str
}

model council Release {
  proposer -> vast,
  adversary -> edge,
  verifier -> local2,
  aggregate unanimous quorum declared on_tie split
}

component Classifier provides out: Answer {
  provide out {
    fn classify(text) = text
  }
}
